it's 1918 four four terrible years more  than 40 countries have been mired in the  bloodshed of the biggest conflict so far  known to man countries across Europe  were caught up in the conflagration but  Africa too was drawn into what was truly  a world war a conflict that changed the  African continent forever this is the  story of the first world war told from  the African perspective  [Music]  more than 2 million Africans were killed  between 1914 and 1918 both civilians and  soldiers many were forced to fight for  their colonial masters France recruited  more Africans than any other colonial  power sending 450,000 troops from West  and North Africa to fight on the front  line in Europe against the Germans  African troops were also deployed on the  continent of Africa itself France still  commemorates the senegalese infantry who  helped to seize the German colony of  Togo the British also fought alongside  African troops against the Germans until  1918 African served as scouts Porter's  and cooks  [Music]  Germany also exploited Africa thousands  were forced into military service in  Tanzania the former German East Africa  that meant labor shortages in the fields  and there was widespread starvation the  economy collapsed around a million  people died in Eastern Africa as a  result the first world war changed the  map of Africa Germany's defeat meant the  loss of its colonies German East Africa  German Cameroon Togo and German  Southwest Africa were all taken over by  the victors as trophies of war  consequences are still being felt today  in Cameroon for example the former  colony was divided between Britain and  France with the French getting more than  four-fifths of the land after the end of  colonial rule in 1960 the divided  country was reunified but by no means  peacefully the english-speaking minority  felt abandoned by the central government  rebels are still fighting for their own  homeland and there are deaths nearly  every day  [Music]  Namibia wants German Southwest Africa  was not divided but placed under the  control of the League of Nations an  independent country was supposed to  emerge with the help of South Africa but  the South African government had other  ideas and ceased control just two years  after the end of the war South Africa  imposed its apartheid regime on the  Libya and oppressed the black population  until Namibia and independence in 1990  the First World War cost millions of  African lives both during the conflict  itself and in the years that followed  Germany's defeat led to the redrawing of  borders colonial power changed hands the  result seismic changes that are still  today at the root of conflicts in many  regions of Africa for many Africans the  end of the First World War did not bring  hope for liberation decades would have  to pass and another world war would have  to be fought before the decolonization  of Africa could finally be celebrated  [Music]
 

